      "review_notes": "The canonical categorical law is mapped to integer labels. The previously selected integer represents one virtual item carrying the processed prefix weight. Conservation of the competing label weights is the central expectation identity. Initial prefix weight zero removes sentinel -1 even for infinite continuation credit. Reviewer feedback moved the rational-coin bias/cast conversion into a private specification helper; its final proof uses an explicit subtype equality followed by the exact existing coin specification. Tests check infinite sentinel credit contributes zero, [0,2,0] has expectation F1 for arbitrary ENNReal F, a leading-zero initial state and generic resource framing."
