      "review_notes": "Discarding the incomplete low prefix t=width%n leaves complete residue cycles rotated by t. Finite rotation and block sums prove each label has equal accepted multiplicity; only finite positive normalization coefficients are cancelled. Rejection occupies at most half the source range, so the CTE proof uses the standard doubled-credit retry. Tests distinguish low-prefix rejection from division rejection: at n5/width8 words0,1,2 are rejected and original word5 returns residue0. The complete numerical kernel, n3/width4 word3 returning0, zero-bit singleton, arbitrary infinite credits and frames are checked."
